<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:26Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Indian workers fill Germany's labor gaps but face hurdles and risks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb798513f146bd5836ccf05095b656e177b42f29fd109882c14a84e4d206e9a7</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-28T06:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882--78ecce9504e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indian-workers-fill-germany-s-labor-gaps-but-face-hurdles-and-risks/a-80072882?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The number of Indians working in Germany has grown rapidly in recent years. But many continue to face challenges in the labor market. Some also fall victim to recruitment scams, leaving them vulnerable to exploitation.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Canada: Supreme Court largely upholds Quebec secularism bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f715f9abca81c50ff3682c508fc0ce47a6a112a60887a9aca84108e8d046a509</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T20:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-supreme-court-largely-upholds-quebec-secularism-bill/a-80082571--e81b43653220.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-supreme-court-largely-upholds-quebec-secularism-bill/a-80082571?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Quebec's government passed Bill 21 to ban religious symbols for public servants, arguing it was necessary to protect its secularist society. Critics argue the bill weakens legal protections for fundamental rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Divisions deepen between EU member states after tense budget summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56d597157d2b5ce822f9c2fd92cbafdf28b35b1499f1f008bbfca5a18a635b73</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T16:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/divisions-deepen-between-eu-member-states-after-tense-budget-summit/a-80078599--05a844bfc611.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/divisions-deepen-between-eu-member-states-after-tense-budget-summit/a-80078599?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An EU leaders summit on the bloc's seven-year budget fell apart amid divisions over how to fund Ukraine. The budget proposal also includes a 3% tax on US tech companies, in a bid for the EU to generate additional funds.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dutch authorities seize 26 critically endangered turtles from luggage of passenger bound for Hong Kong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ececd39328bd8454560018c7a384090ad7af8f954e02898333782fce1b782d65</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-ko/a-80077824--bdef9f0677e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-kong/a-80077824?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The tiny Vallarta mud turtle was only discovered in 2018. It's critically endangered with around 300 thought to live in the wild. Almost one tenth of that number were stashed in a traveler's luggage, bound in duct tape.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Airline Norse Atlantic files for bankruptcy, succumbing to aviation fuel costs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7e6ad29d5191fd0a7f802a5b97661a56d48dc655b873e222aafb18c5f67e288</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728--deb84ffc1870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airline-norse-atlantic-files-for-bankruptcy-succumbing-to-aviation-fuel-costs/a-80076728?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The low-cost airline was only founded a few years ago and had been struggling to turn a profit. The spike in aviation fuel prices caused by the war in Iran has now driven Norway's Norse Atlantic into bankruptcy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Gambia gears up for election, can Barrow secure a third term?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65d2e6e8f18d41eeac2d67ff48a316fac8bdfa457317e2e44ce0e15eaef24257</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340--b6856a8ea5b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-gambia-gears-up-for-election-can-barrow-secure-a-third-term/a-80076340?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Adama Barrow is seeking a third term as Gambians vote on December 5. The election will test the opposition's appeal and the country's progress on democratic reform.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Informer TV owner Vucicevic arrested: Has the reckoning with Serbia's pro-Vucic media machine begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d18cdfb63f4d5f7f9ea74d10cf7623d18ca79f798b20916f7c9e0e621067c547</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:07:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/informer-tv-owner-vucicevic-arrested-has-the-reckoning-with-serbia-s-pro-vucic-media-machine-begun/a-80074650--983ff7ae64ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/informer-tv-owner-vucicevic-arrested-has-the-reckoning-with-serbia-s-pro-vucic-media-machine-begun/a-80074650?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The arrest of media owner Dragan J. Vucicevic raises questions about whether Serbia is holding the people behind the country's pro-Vucic media accountable — or whether this is another political power struggle.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Duterte's ICC trial: What is at stake for the Philippines?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f94aad53a777af3b9e142261157526942fdbd552da8bf7cc2b960a9619d3a7a</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657--9d6c676a2419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte faces trial in The Hague over his deadly war on drugs. The proceedings could determine the political fortunes of a powerful dynasty. Victims' families hope to see justice.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Iran, child marriage risks complicated by war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7deaf1f81957faea92a395d15e12ebd230a37db601ed32b8aeedaa9dc421659</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-iran-child-marriage-risks-complicated-by-war/a-80075473--2a4ac067a146.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-iran-child-marriage-risks-complicated-by-war/a-80075473?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">War, poverty and disrupted schooling could put more girls in Iran at risk of child marriage, rights advocates have warned.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Albania's youth are protesting, no longer leaving the country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b236aa501b07323c386d8b601aa189370a9b774b7baac112c8f7a3efe2c49f7b</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T20:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-s-youth-are-protesting-no-longer-leaving-the-country/a-80068939--19bf6b73472f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-s-youth-are-protesting-no-longer-leaving-the-country/a-80068939?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Youth protests against a rigid political system and corruption have shaken the government of Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama. They also show that fewer young people are willing to emigrate in search of a better future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi pop music is thriving — but for the right reasons?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a66c7da769a72d01e9fadbabe9d4ecd2e5eacf4ff75869b1c00f324b6cba883</id><updated>2026-11-28T08:06:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T17:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-pop-music-is-thriving-but-for-the-right-reasons/a-80036013--30f0e598eb37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-pop-music-is-thriving-but-for-the-right-reasons/a-80036013?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As part of Vision 2030, Saudi Arabia's music scene has evolved hugely thanks to state funding and support. Local musicians and DJs are optimistic. But are they actually just helping prop up an authoritarian 